# Field language (talk to a researcher)

Speak in conventional video-generation / streaming terms. Do not
invent project slang and then force the user to learn it.

**Required names**

| Say | Do not say (in new speech) | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| **context frames** | leftover, leftover slice, leftover well | Real visual prefix already observed (V2V history). |
| **KV cache** | memory, fast memory (unless you mean \(W_{\text{fast}}\)) | Attention K/V window. If you mean something else, name that thing. |
| **context-frame representation** (or scene embedding / scene prototype of the context frames) | well, scene well | Compact code of the context frames. **Not** fast weights. |
| **fast weights** / \(W_{\text{fast}}\) | well | TTT / Titans / delta-rule parameters. **Not** this method. |
| **sink** | only when you mean the Forcing-paper KV sink (static / EMA) | First-frame or EMA of evicted **KV** tokens. |

Code and old tables may still say `leftover`. When talking to the
user, say **context frames**. Do not ask them to adopt our slang.

The context-frame representation paper is **dropped** (too thin).
Current method: **prefix-protected fast weights** — update /
protect / fork. Do not call that a well. Do not title
“motion = spread.”
